r. If you bet, you risk being raised by stronger hands (like 9-x, 2-2, 3-3, or even a completed flush draw if they had two spades). Going all-in (-2) is overly aggressive with such a weak current hand and too risky. Folding (-1) is incorrect because you have strong drawing equity. Raising to 100 or more could be a semi-bluff, but without prior initiative, it may not succeed often.\n\nBest line: **Check (0)** to see how opponent acts — if they bet, you can call (possibly with odds to draw); if they check back, you see free card.\n\nReason:  \nChecking preserves your drawing equity, avoids bloating the pot with a vulnerable hand, and allows you to make a better decision on the turn based on opponent's action. It’s low-risk and consistent with balanced post-flop strategy in a checked-through pot.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
